  total wall 903.2s

  HONEST FRAMING (report as-is):
  - FM-PINN and L1 grid-search: comparable on single-alpha (not 'better').
  - DFA/Hurst: COMPARABLE accuracy too, from a 1D path with NO density/IC/
    transient. So FM-PINN is NOT justified by single-alpha accuracy.
  - FM-PINN's real advantage = what DFA/Hurst CANNOT do: joint alpha+gamma+D
    recovery, a calibrated uncertainty interval, and a full valid density.
  - LSQ-residual fails under noise; fixed-alpha=1 is the no-memory null.
  - Real S&P: volatility clustering significant; decay-shape favors exponential.
